  "articleBody": "When you're thinking about an exterior entry ramp, it's not just a one-size-fits-all situation. There are a few things to consider to make sure you pick the best ramp for your specific needs. First, think about the space you have available. This is critical because it directly impacts the ramp's length and configuration. Next, consider the user's mobility device – is it a wheelchair, scooter, or something else? This will influence the ramp's width and load capacity. Then, you'll need to decide on the ramp type and material. Modular residential aluminum ramps are quite popular and can range anywhere from around $1,000 to over $10,000, depending on the size and complexity. Commercial modular systems, on the other hand, often start at $5,000 and can go well over $20,000. And of course, budget is always a factor. If your situation involves code compliance, complex site conditions, or structural attachments, bringing in a qualified professional is a really smart move. They can ensure your ramp meets all the required load and accessibility standards. HH Remodeling LLC can help you explore your options and make the best choice for your home in the Denver metro area, ensuring your ramp is safe, functional, and built to last. Give us a call at 303-505-0866 for a consultation.",
